---
layout: base.njk
title: "Submit IOC/Profile"
description: "Submit a new indicator of compromise, a new DPRK actor profile lead, or a general tip for manual review."
---
{#
  src/submit/index.njk: backend-free. Submissions go by mailto link, never a
  form POST or a JS-built URL (a long profile_sources list can exceed the
  ~2000-character URL limit); each is turned into a draft by hand
  (docs/submission-review-assist.md). The address is read from
  src/_data/site.json `businessEmail`; do not hardcode it elsewhere.
#}
{% set mailSubject = "New Chollima Hunter submission" %}
{% set mailBody %}Submission type (New IOC / New Profile / Correction or removal request / General tip):

Your contact (optional, only used to follow up on this submission):

Description (what you're submitting, and why you believe it's DPRK-linked):


--- If this is a new IOC, also fill in ---
Indicator type (email address, phone number, GitHub, LinkedIn or other
platform account, persona name, npm or PyPI package, file hash, domain, IP
address, wallet or smart contract address, or other):
Indicator value:
Associated campaign/cluster (if known):

--- If this is a correction or removal request, also fill in ---
Page address:
What is wrong, or why the entry concerns your own identity:
Public record supporting the correction (if any):
--- If this is a new profile lead, also fill in ---
Subject name / known aliases:
Alleged activity:
Links to supporting public sources (one per line; required for any claim
about a named person):
{% endset %}
<section>
  <h1>Submit IOC/Profile</h1>
  <p>
    Send an indicator, a profile lead, a correction or removal request, or a
    tip by email. Every submission is reviewed manually; nothing is published
    automatically. If you are listed, see
    <a href="/guidance/#listed">If you are listed on this site</a>.
  </p>

{% if site.businessEmail and "TODO" not in site.businessEmail %}
  <p>
    A submission is an ordinary email to
    <a href="mailto:{{ site.businessEmail }}">{{ site.businessEmail }}</a>; it
    never passes through the site.
    {%- if site.repoUrl %} Corrections and removal requests can also be raised
    as an issue on the {% set externalLink = { url: site.repoUrl + "/issues", text: "GitHub repository" } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %}.
    {%- endif %}
  </p>

  <p>
    <a class="btn" href="mailto:{{ site.businessEmail }}?subject={{ mailSubject | urlencode }}&amp;body={{ mailBody | trim | urlencode }}">Email your submission</a>
  </p>
  <p class="form-hint">
    The link opens your mail client with the template below filled in.
  </p>

  {% set disclaimer = {
    title: "What not to send",
    id: "what-not-to-send",
    body: 'Do not attach malware; send the file hash and a link to published analysis. Do not include other people&rsquo;s personal data beyond what identifies the entry. Email is not confidential.'
  } %}{% include "partials/disclaimer.njk" %}

  <fieldset class="form-fieldset">
    <legend>Email template</legend>
    <pre class="query-block">{{ mailBody | trim }}</pre>
  </fieldset>

  <fieldset class="form-fieldset">
    <legend>New profile leads</legend>
    <p class="form-hint">
      <strong>A claim about a named individual needs a public source</strong>,
      such as an indictment, sanctions designation, press release or named
      threat-intelligence report. Without one it will not be published.
    </p>
  </fieldset>
{% else %}
  {% set disclaimer = {
    title: "Submissions are not open yet",
    body: 'This page is not accepting submissions yet.'
  } %}{% include "partials/disclaimer.njk" %}
  {%- if site.repoUrl %}
  <p>
    In the meantime, open an issue on the {% set externalLink = { url: site.repoUrl + "/issues", text: "GitHub repository" } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %}
    with the indicator or lead and its public source.
  </p>
  {%- endif %}
{% endif %}
</section>
